{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":36.0099983215332,"text":"A pine cone of bronze, almost four meters tall, stands in a niche at the end of the courtyard named after it. The Romans made it in the first century A.D. as a fountain. Water came out of the holes between its scales. It stood near the Pantheon, beside a temple of the Egyptian goddess Isis. In the Middle Ages, it was moved to the courtyard of the old Basilica of St. Peter, where the poet Dante saw it and used it in his Inferno to describe how big a giant's face was. It has been here since 1608. The two bronze peacocks beside it are copies of the ones that decorated Hadrian's tomb.","words":[{"word":"A","start":0,"end":0.47999998927116394},{"word":"pine","start":0.47999998927116394,"end":0.7799999713897705},{"word":"cone","start":0.7799999713897705,"end":0.9399999976158142},{"word":"of","start":0.9399999976158142,"end":1.659999966621399},{"word":"bronze","start":1.659999966621399,"end":1.659999966621399},{"word":"almost","start":2.200000047683716,"end":2.259999990463257},{"word":"four","start":2.259999990463257,"end":2.6600000858306885},{"word":"meters","start":2.6600000858306885,"end":2.940000057220459},{"word":"tall","start":2.940000057220459,"end":3.3399999141693115},{"word":"stands","start":4.039999961853027,"end":4.059999942779541},{"word":"in","start":4.059999942779541,"end":4.28000020980835},{"word":"a","start":4.28000020980835,"end":4.599999904632568},{"word":"niche","start":4.599999904632568,"end":4.599999904632568},{"word":"at","start":4.599999904632568,"end":4.820000171661377},{"word":"the","start":4.820000171661377,"end":5.059999942779541},{"word":"end","start":5.059999942779541,"end":5.179999828338623},{"word":"of","start":5.179999828338623,"end":5.320000171661377},{"word":"the","start":5.320000171661377,"end":5.480000019073486},{"word":"courtyard","start":5.480000019073486,"end":5.820000171661377},{"word":"named","start":5.820000171661377,"end":6.179999828338623},{"word":"afte